    { "id": 9, "sev": "P2", "loc": "clearCheckpointManager not exported", "note": "PARTIAL — exported from tools index (the concrete gap). Wiring it into teardown belongs in the session-lifecycle owner (CLI serve / channels), NOT the recursive agent-loop finally (which runs per-recursion-level and would wipe state mid-run). LRU bound prevents growth meanwhile." }
  ],
  "fixed_in_005_6": [
    { "id": 2, "sev": "P1", "loc": "subagent session scoping", "note": "FIXED — subagents enter their own withSession(randomUUID) alongside withWorkspace; Date.now() (which collided for parallel same-ms spawns) replaced with a UUID. Task/tx/scratchpad stores isolated from parent + siblings." },
    { "id": 6, "sev": "P1", "loc": "transaction rollback safety regression", "note": "FIXED — recordTransactionFile hashes each file as written; rollback refuses to revert a file that diverged since (concurrent edit), so it can't clobber another session's committed work. Real-file test proves the refusal + survival." },
    { "id": 8, "sev": "P2", "loc": "transaction allocation/eviction", "note": "FIXED — read/record paths don't allocate (peekTx); commit/rollback release the entry; LRU eviction skips ACTIVE transactions." }
  ],
  "remaining_005_6": [
    { "id": 1, "sev": "P1", "loc": "scope key = persistent sessionId, not per-run id", "note": "The two-key redesign (per-run id for ephemeral tasks/tx/scratchpad/foreground-handlers + logical session id for background mailboxes). PRACTICAL IMPACT limited to CONCURRENT TURNS on the SAME session — which most harnesses serialize (distinct sessions are already isolated). Getting the run-vs-session split wrong could break legitimate multi-turn state (undo/tasks across turns), so it's deliberate design work, not a rushed pass. Genuinely open." },
