{"fixes":[{"id":"a","status":"not-resolved","note":"The hash is not atomically tied to the session's write. file_write awaits other imports before recordTransactionFile re-reads the path, so another session can write first; the original session then records the later session's hash and rollback may accept it and clobber that edit. Rollback also has a check-to-revert TOCTOU window, and null/empty hashes or an unreadable/deleted current file bypass divergence protection entirely."},{"id":"b","status":"resolved","note":"Read/record paths use peekTx without allocating; successful commit and rollback delete only the current session's state; eviction scans for an inactive entry and never removes an active transaction. The cap intentionally becomes soft when all entries are active."},{"id":"c","status":"resolved","note":"randomUUID removes same-millisecond collisions. withSession is correctly nested inside withWorkspace and covers streamText creation, stream consumption, retries, and tool execution; the closing parentheses correctly unwind the inner session callback and outer workspace callback."}],"new_P0_P1":[]}
